# Build context sent to the Docker daemon (and uploaded by Railway).
#
# Without this the context includes every node_modules in the monorepo plus
# bundled Bible assets — hundreds of megabytes, uploaded on every deploy. The
# image installs its own dependencies from the lockfile, so none of it is
# wanted, and a host node_modules can carry platform-specific binaries that
# break inside a Linux container.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — rebuilt inside the image
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
release
**/release
.next
out
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
**/.turbo
apps/desktop/build-tmp

# Secrets — must never enter an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Desktop-only assets the API has no use for
apps/desktop
apps/mobile
packages/bible-engine/Bibles
packages/bible-engine/Backgrounds
packages/bible-engine/NDI
.bible-src

# Local tooling and history
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs and scratch files
docs
*.md
!README.md
prisma-test.mjs
run-backend.mjs
swagger2.json
